# Product Safety And Figma

- Keep feedback rules rules-based for MVP 1.0 unless the user explicitly changes product direction.
- Do not add AI diagnosis or medical claims without explicit approval.
- Prefer neutral phrasing such as `check in`, `follow up`, or `consider contacting your vet`.
- Figma should refine visuals and UX structure, not override business rules, schema, or product logic.
- When implementing from Figma, map designs into the existing feature and component structure instead of generating one-off fragments.
- Reuse existing components and naming conventions whenever possible.
- If a design conflicts with product logic or documented rules, preserve the documented product behavior and flag the mismatch.
